  "summary": "Justification is God's righteous verdict that declares sinners right with him by grace through faith in Christ.",
  "historical_context": "Paul frames justification with courtroom and covenant language, especially through Abraham and the law.",
  "ancient_near_east_context": "Ancient courts issued verdicts that established status, and Scripture uses that legal language for God's saving declaration.",
  "literary_context": "Justification is developed most fully in Romans and Galatians and is echoed in the Psalms, Prophets, and New Testament witness.",
  "covenantal_significance": "Justification secures right standing with God on the basis of his promise and Christ's work, not human merit.",
